Theorem TF-9a: CollectionReuse transfer produces FRESH(CollectionBuffer)

  Preconditions:
    - Instruction is `CollectionReuse { old_var, args }` per Annex E §AIMS TF-9a + Appendix A row 10
    - `old_var` is a dying collection (list, set, or map) whose buffer
      backing can be reused by RL-11 structural pairing
    - FRESH(CollectionBuffer) = `(Owned, Linear, Once, Unique, BlockLocal,
      CollectionBuffer, {may_alloc=true})` per §3 TF-9a + Appendix A
    - Shape is ALWAYS CollectionBuffer (distinct from ReusableCtor variants
      handled by TF-9; distinct from NonReusable + ContextHole)

  Soundness property:
    Forall CollectionReuse { old_var, args }.
      transfer_tf9a(CollectionReuse) = FRESH(CollectionBuffer)
    AND L-6 layer (b) monotonicity holds: TF-9a is a constant function on
    the static instruction shape; for ANY pair (a, b) of input states with
    a ≤ b, f(a) = f(b) = FRESH(CollectionBuffer), hence f(a) ≤ f(b) by
    L-4 reflexivity.

  Proof obligation:
    Three-part discharge:
      (a) Output enumeration — verify all 7 per-dimension columns of
          Appendix A row 10 are emitted:
            access = Owned; consumption = Linear; cardinality = Once;
            uniqueness = Unique; locality = BlockLocal;
            shape = CollectionBuffer; effect = {may_alloc} = 0b001.
      (b) Shape constraint — verify shape is ALWAYS CollectionBuffer;
          CollectionReuse NEVER emits ReusableStruct / ReusableEnum /
          NonReusable / ContextHole. The CollectionBuffer shape is the
          discriminating mark for {List,Set,Map}Literal allocations
          per Annex E §AIMS Shape lattice.
      (c) L-6 layer (b) monotonicity — TF-9a is a constant function on
          input AimsState. For ANY pair (a, b) with a ≤ b,
          f(a) = f(b) = FRESH(CollectionBuffer), hence f(a) ≤ f(b) by
          L-4 reflexivity.

    Part (a) — per-dimension column verification:
      access = Owned — reused buffer owned by the result.
      consumption = Linear — fresh buffer slot, exactly-once consumed.
      cardinality = Once — fresh allocation; downstream uses via TF-11.
      uniqueness = Unique — RC = 1 invariant inherited from old_var's
        unique state (RL-11 + DP-6 require source Unique).
      locality = BlockLocal — CollectionReuse fires within same-block
        scope or dominator-validated cross-block region.
      shape = CollectionBuffer — fixed by the CollectionReuse instruction
        kind; distinguishes from ReusableCtor variants per §1.6.
      effect = {may_alloc=true} = 0b001 — buffer-equivalent allocation
        at AIMS layer.

    Part (b) — shape-CollectionBuffer invariant:
      Appendix A row 10 column "Shape" reads "CollectionBuffer" verbatim.
      Verified: transfer_tf9a() emits shape = "CollectionBuffer"
      exclusively. Negative witness: no branch emits ReusableStruct,
      ReusableEnum, NonReusable, or ContextHole.

    Part (c) — constant-function monotonicity:
      For ANY input state (a, b) in (AimsState union {SCALAR})^2 with
      a ≤ b: TF-9a reads NOTHING from `a` — output is determined ONLY
      by the CollectionReuse instruction kind. f(a) = FRESH
      (CollectionBuffer) = f(b). By L-4 reflexivity,
      FRESH(CollectionBuffer) ≤ FRESH(CollectionBuffer) on the product
      order (componentwise on each of the 7 dimensions).
      Verified via product_le(fresh("CollectionBuffer"),
      fresh("CollectionBuffer")) = Some(true).

    Engines dispatched:
      monotonicity (PRIMARY — L-6 layer (b) per-instance constant-function
        check per section_04::verify_tf9a_collectionreuse_fresh_collectionbuffer)
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — Appendix A row 10 forward-transfer-matrix
        enumeration + shape-CollectionBuffer invariant per
        section_04::verify_tf9a_collectionreuse_fresh_collectionbuffer)
      lattice (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully; product-order at §02)
      refinement (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully; TF-9a emits FRESH
        directly, not via refine())

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_04 monotonicity + case_analysis engines discharge TF-9a via per-dimension Appendix A row 10 enumeration + shape-CollectionBuffer invariant + constant-function monotonicity check
